/target
# The iOS cross-build's own CARGO_TARGET_DIR; see ios/Makefile.
/target-ios
/coverage
/lcov.info
# cargo-mutants writes its whole scratch build tree here, and rotates the
# previous run alongside it.
/mutants.out
/mutants.out.old
*.jks
.env
# Generated by the Android NDK toolchain setup; nothing checks it in.
/.cargo/android-ndk-wrapper.cmake
# `/.cargo/config.toml` used to be ignored here. It was, at the time, purely a
# leftover: a20f868 deleted the 32-bit Android linker config and ignored the
# path so a stale local copy could not come back. Nothing generates that file
# today, and it is now the tree's only home for the Apple deployment floors —
# which are the definition of a setting that must be identical for every
# developer and every CI row. An ignore rule on it means the fix for a silent
# runtime failure is itself dropped silently.
/.claude/worktrees/
